{"aggregate_id": "01M5099074FJD67YSY2EH661NK", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01M509908X03BD0B5T2P2314DA", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"actor": "kentgale@gmail.com", "created_at": "2026-10-15T17:20:36.618791+00:00", "friendly_name": "Off-host dead-man pings for the on-host watchers", "mission_id": "01M5099074FJD67YSY2EH661NK", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "offhost-deadman-pings-01M50990", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "felix-canary and felix-health-check watch each other (#1063) but share one host, one user manager, one checkout and one ntfy topic, so losing any of them silences both. RFC #1069 decided that both watchers ping a hosted dead-man service (healthchecks.io) after each successful run and send a fail ping when an alert cannot be delivered; the service emails Kent, never through ntfy. Ping URLs are capability secrets kept on office2, never in the repo. Tracks kentonium3/kg-automation#1077.", "purpose_tldr": "If office2, its user manager, the checkout or the ntfy alert channel goes down, Kent still gets an email, because the two on-host watchers stop pinging a hosted dead-man service.", "target_branch": "feat/offhost-deadman-pings", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "kg-automation", "project_uuid": "2c011d09-8272-470c-b9e2-e9ccf8ad3fbd", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-10-15T17:20:36.637758+00:00"}
